<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Clusium</h1><p class="st-meta">900 BCE – 295 BCE (approx.) · capital Clusium</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Inland Etruscan city whose king Lars Porsenna, in Roman tradition, besieged Rome after the expulsion of the Tarquins.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Clusium, Etruscan Clevsin, modern Chiusi, overlooked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/val-di-chiana">Val di Chiana</a>, a fertile corridor linking central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruria">Etruria</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiber-river">Tiber</a> valley. It developed from Villanovan settlements and flourished from the 7th century BCE, when its distinctive canopic urns, cinerary jars with human-headed lids, show a local elite of growing wealth.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Clusium's power rested on agriculture in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/val-di-chiana">Chiana</a> valley and on control of routes towards the interior. Its workshops produced cinerary urns, sculptures in local stone and fine bucchero pottery, while painted tombs such as the Tomb of the Monkey show banquets and games. Roman tradition records its king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lars-porsenna">Lars Porsenna</a>, who attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> around 508 BCE and possibly took it.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 391 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauls">Gauls</a> attacked Clusium, an event Roman writers linked to the Gallic sack of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. The city came under Roman control after the wars of the early 3rd century, traditionally around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sentinum">battle of Sentinum</a> in 295 BCE, and remained a modest Roman town; Etruscan burials continued there into the 1st century BCE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 900 BCE – 295 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">